{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And Jacob saw.</b> Because sensations are joined in one place, they exchange with one another, as in \"See the smell of my son\" (Genesis 27:27), and \"sweet is the light\" (Ecclesiastes 11:7). So too \"and Jacob saw,\" for after it is written \"here I have heard\" (v. 2)." "<b>Why do you look.</b> That you have wealth, or do not be quarreling one with another, like \"we will look at each other's faces\" (2 Chronicles 25:17)."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 42, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:47:48.848235887Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}